        "original_id": "123fa44b-9b67-5ac1-ac43-cee71b842858",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Nicholas Amer, William Shakespeare\n- Places: Tranmere, Birkenhead, Cheshire\n- Works: The Tempest\n- Topics: acting careers, Shakespeare plays\n\nFacts:\n- William Shakespeare wrote The Tempest, a play believed to have been written in 1610–11, and many critics consider it the last play he wrote alone.\n- Nicholas Amer was born Thomas Harold Amer on 29 September 1923 in Tranmere, Birkenhead, Cheshire.\n- Nicholas Amer is an English stage, film, and television actor known for performances in William Shakespeare's plays.\n- Nicholas Amer made his professional debut in 1948 as Ferdinand in The Tempest.",
